---
permalink: /sitemap.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
layout: null
---
{#-
  Every page worth finding, for the crawlers that ask.

  Two lists, because the site builds its pages two ways and neither one knows
  about the other:

  - `collections.all` is every template the build rendered, so a new game, a
    new content type or a new page is in here the moment the file exists.
  - the glossary term pages are paginated out of `glossaryTerms` and set
    `eleventyExcludeFromCollections`, which is what keeps forty of them out of
    every collection the nav and the palette read. That flag is about
    collections, not about being findable, so they are added here from the same
    data their pages are generated from — `term.url` is the permalink, not a
    second guess at it.

  What is left out:

  - anything marked `noIndex`, which is the same flag that writes the page's
    own `noindex` tag: My Reference, which holds nothing until a reader's
    browser fills it in, the accounts page, and every page of an unlisted game.
  - 404 and the viewport probe, which set `eleventyExcludeFromCollections` in
    their own frontmatter and so never arrive in the first list.
  - hidden games, which `buildGames` drops before anything downstream knows
    they exist.

  An unlisted game's glossary terms need saying twice, because the second list
  does not carry the `noIndex` the first one does — the visibility is read from
  the registry instead.

  The two lists overlap by exactly one page, and `unique` is what settles it:
  Eleventy puts the first page of a paginated template into `collections.all`
  whatever its computed `eleventyExcludeFromCollections` says, so the first
  glossary term in the first game arrives down both paths. Sorted as well as
  deduplicated, so the file is stable between builds and a diff of it is worth
  reading.

  No `lastmod`. The honest value is when a page's content last changed, and the
  build knows only when it last ran; stamping today on all of it every deploy
  claims everything changed, which is worth less than saying nothing.
-#}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
{% set urls = [] -%}
{%- for item in collections.all -%}
  {%- if not item.data.noIndex -%}{%- set _ = urls.push(item.url) -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for term in glossaryTerms -%}
  {%- if games[term.gameSlug].visibility == "listed" -%}{%- set _ = urls.push(term.url) -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for url in urls | unique | sort %}
  <url><loc>{{ site.url }}{{ url | basePath }}</loc></url>
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
